  "design_intent": "Two strategies: (1) the $15 Gallery Cafe lunch and walk everywhere ($44), or (2) the $5 hawker lunch, which is too far from the Art Museum to walk and still make the 15:00 meeting, forcing one $12 taxi ($46 = budget). The afternoon is the same in every solution: meet at the jetty at exactly 15:00, then Summit Garden and Cable Car (riding the cable car requires the garden; the Waterfront Lookout alternative needs taxis and breaks the budget), then walk home leaving at 17:00 in rush hour (23 min, just under the 25-minute walk cap), arriving 17:23. Traps: the friend's text contradicts the fixed 15:00 meeting, the Design Annex must come directly after the Art Museum, only one temple may be visited, taxis cannot serve the Old Market, and the pass must be collected at V before the museum.",
